ruyiseek (0.1.0-15) unstable; urgency=high

  * Watch every successfully scanned directory with Linux inotify. Creating,
    deleting or renaming files now rebuilds the in-memory index in the
    background, so newly created Chinese filenames such as 中文.txt become
    searchable without restarting the daemon.
  * Keep mount discovery and explicit --root mode on the same refresh path,
    retain the old index while rebuilding, and schedule a follow-up pass when
    a filesystem event races with a scan.
  * Add a five-minute fallback refresh for unwatched directories or exhausted
    inotify limits, while avoiding rebuilds for content-only file writes.
  * Reap a UI-spawned daemon when it exits so stopping it from the CLI no
    longer leaves a zombie child behind while the UI remains open.
  * Serialize the two X11 clipboard round-trip tests because a display has one
    CLIPBOARD selection and parallel tests otherwise steal it from each other.

