ruyiseek (0.1.0-12) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix external-volume search on UOS. When started without explicit
    --root arguments, ruyiseekd now reads /proc/self/mountinfo and indexes
    HOME plus readable local block-device mounts. OS trees, pseudo and
    network filesystems, loop/squashfs mounts and duplicate bind mounts are
    excluded; escaped and non-UTF-8 mount paths are decoded as Linux path
    bytes.
  * Detect mount and unmount changes every two seconds. A replacement index
    is built in the background while the previous index remains searchable,
    then swapped atomically. Nested mounts under HOME are treated as scan
    boundaries so their contents are not duplicated.
  * Scale the automatic item budget to 250,000 entries per discovered root,
    capped at 2,000,000. Explicit --max-entries remains a global override and
    explicit --root keeps its deterministic opt-out semantics.
  * Add focused tests for UOS mountinfo parsing, filtering, path escapes,
    bind/overlapping-root deduplication, automatic budgets and CLI behavior.
  * Normalize the v0.1.0-11 Rust sources with the repository's Rust 1.75
    rustfmt baseline so GitHub CI proceeds past its formatting gate.
  * Run CI tests and Clippy on the native GNU target instead of inheriting the
    musl release target without its standard library or release toolchain.
  * Fix the v0.1.0-11 X11 clipboard TARGETS array lifetime for Rust 1.75;
    keep the fixed-size atom array by value instead of borrowing temporaries.
  * Repair the X11 clipboard integration test: call the real in-process owner
    instead of a nonexistent helper binary, remove invalid placeholder polling,
    and compile the test only when the x11 feature is enabled.
  * Resolve strict Clippy findings in the X11 platform layer, including checked
    property lengths, checked Instant subtraction and public API documentation.
  * Remove redundant character-test closures in the query scorer for the
    workspace-wide strict Clippy gate.
  * Clean the standalone clipboard round-trip example for strict Clippy while
    retaining its linear, protocol-demonstration structure.
  * Finish the Rust 1.75 strict-Clippy pass for UI callback ownership, path
    APIs, detached daemon startup and integer-rendered tray icon gradients.

