ruyiseek (0.1.0-10) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Offline-friendly install. The .deb no longer Requires libx11-6,
    libxcb1, libxi6, libxcursor1, libx11-xcb1, libxkbcommon0,
    libfontconfig1, libstdc++6 — every shared library ruyiseek-ui needs
    at runtime (28 files: glibc base stack + X11 client stack + font
    stack, totalling ~268 KiB plus the dynamic linker) is now bundled
    into /usr/lib/ruyiseek/ and the binary's PT_INTERP / DT_RPATH are
    rewritten by patchelf to that path. Install on a target machine
    with no network access to apt mirrors now works without any
    Depends-driven `apt install` fetch. Depends is reduced to a single
    package, libc6 (>= 2.28), which is present on every supported
    base (UOS 20 / DDE / Debian 10+) and only exists as a sanity
    guard.
  * packaging/deb/bundle-libs.sh is the new entry point. It walks
    the transitive closure of SONAME deps starting from the original
    Depends list plus libstdc++/libgcc_s (used by the C++ fontconfig
    shim and Rust runtime), copies each (preserving SONAME symlinks
    with cp -P), copies the real ld-2.28.so file behind the
    ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 symlink (so the PT_INTERP target is not a
    dangling link on the target machine), and patchelfs
    ruyiseek-ui's interpreter + rpath to /usr/lib/ruyiseek. A
    post-patch ldd self-check fails the build if any closure entry
    ends up unresolvable.
  * packaging/deb/recursive_ldd.sh (the closure walker used by
    bundle-libs.sh) resolves SONAMEs via ldconfig -p with a
    find-fallback, parses ldd output to enqueue child SONAMEs, and
    marks MISSING / MISSING-DEP on stderr for anything that can't be
    located.
  * build.sh is updated to call bundle-libs.sh after install and to
    skip-delete the new *.sh helpers from the staging tree cleanup
    pass (they live next to build.sh as build-time only).
  * Verify pass on a fresh dpkg -i install:
      ldd /usr/bin/ruyiseek-ui                (rpath honored)
      /usr/lib/ruyiseek/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 --library-path \
          /usr/lib/ruyiseek /usr/bin/ruyiseek-ui --help   (rc=0)

