ruyiseek (0.1.0-9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Click outside the launcher to hide. The launcher window is now
    960x600, no-frame, always-on-top, and transparent between the
    rounded card and the screen edges. A full-window TouchArea sits
    below the focus-scope in z-order and is the only thing that
    catches clicks on the empty backdrop; a separate TouchArea on the
    card itself sits below the result rows and search input and
    forwards focus back to the LineEdit when the user clicks on card
    padding. Together they make: click outside -> dismiss; click on
    card padding -> re-focus search; click on result row / search
    input -> the existing handlers (activate / caret move). All
    passes through the existing root.dismiss() callback so the D-Bus
    session lock and idle rearm logic stay untouched.
  * New icon. packaging/icons/io.github.ethanbird.RuyiSeek.svg is a
    minimal magnifying glass with a teal-to-deep-teal linear gradient
    (#2a8aa3 -> #176b87) that matches the launcher's accent color.
    packacking/deb/build.sh installs:
      - /usr/share/icons/hicolor/scalable/apps/<name>.svg
      - /usr/share/icons/hicolor/{48,64,128,256}x{...}/apps/<name>.png
        (rendered at build time with rsvg-convert, not committed)
    The system tray icon (KSNI) does not load files so
    apps/ruyiseek-ui/src/tray.rs::make_icon() is rewritten to match
    the SVG palette: transparent background, gradient ring + handle
    instead of the previous teal disc with a white ring. The unit
    test generated_icon_has_argb_pixels_and_expected_colors now
    verifies both gradient endpoints are present and the legacy
    white ring color is gone.
  * Minimalist search bar. The 42px "寻" icon and the 66x28 "Ctrl x2"
    hint chip are removed from the launcher; the search bar is now a
    single 720px-wide LineEdit with an ellipsis-trimmed placeholder
    ("搜索文件、文件夹、应用或命令..."). The focus-scope height
    formula drops from 122 + N*54 to 110 + N*54 to reflect the
    shorter search bar, and the focus-scope is centered in the
    960x600 window with x/y bindings so the card sits in the visual
    middle on any screen size.
  * Settings panel centering. The SettingsPanel is now a fixed
    640x480 Rectangle with explicit x/y bindings to the window
    center, so it no longer hugs the top-left corner of the screen.
    The right-click context menu positions itself relative to the
    focus-scope (x = focus-scope.x + 12, y = focus-scope.y + 82 + N*46)
    so it lines up with the result row that was clicked regardless
    of where the card sits in the window.
  * Escape now hides the launcher directly. The previous
    "clear-then-hide" two-step on Esc is replaced with a single
    root.dismiss() call, so a stray Esc does not leave an empty
    input + a hidden window. Users who still want to clear the
    input without hiding can use Ctrl+L or select-and-delete.
  * Bug fix: re-summoning the launcher with a second double-Ctrl no
    longer keeps the previous result list visible. The Slint
    LineEdit's edited() callback only fires on user input, so a
    programmatic set_query("") does not by itself clear results.
    show_launcher() and apply_desktop_action() now take the
    result-paths + generation handles explicitly and:
      - reset results to an empty Model
      - clear result_paths
      - reset selected-index to 0
      - reset query to ""
      - bump the search-response generation so any in-flight
        callback from the daemon is discarded
      - reset status text to the idle message
    The second double-Ctrl therefore starts on a clean slate
    instead of showing the previous results while the new query
    is still in flight.

