ruyiseek (0.1.0-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Make the UI binary auto-start the ruyiseekd daemon if it is not
    already running. Previously a fresh install (or a daemon that was
    killed) would surface "无法连接后台服务：..." in the status bar
    because the launcher's Exec= /usr/bin/ruyiseek-ui only started the
    UI, never the daemon. Now ruyiseek-ui probes the socket on startup
    and, if it is unreachable, spawns the sibling ruyiseekd binary,
    waits up to 5 s for it to bind, then proceeds. The daemon is
    forked as a detached child (its std::process::Child handle is
    dropped so the OS reparents it to PID 1 when the UI exits), so
    closing the UI no longer takes the indexer down with it.
  * Install flow: install .deb → click launcher → daemon and UI both
    come up with no extra steps. Users who already manage ruyiseekd
    via systemd --user see no change (the probe returns early).
  * Best-effort: any failure to start the daemon is logged to stderr
    but does not abort the UI; the existing "无法连接后台服务" status
    bar message is still shown in that case.

